{
 "_meta": {
  "table": "rpt_ads_performance_hourly",
  "report_type": "ads-performance-v1",
  "is_snapshot": false,
  "description": "Amazon Ads performance at Amazon's own record grain (Marketing Stream ads-performance-v1): one row per marketplace-local hour per combination of every dimension Amazon delivers — campaign, ad group, ad, target, search term, placement, advertised product, conversion source — for Sponsored Products, Brands, Display and Television alike (ad_product says which). `hour` is the marketplace's own local hour (dayparting: GROUP BY weekday, hour); window_start_utc is that hour as an instant. Metrics carry Amazon's v1 names snake-cased — one exception, metric.5secondViewsVideoAd → five_second_views_video_ad — and every other non-zero metric is in `extra` under Amazon's own name; the last 75 days are kept.",
  "search_aliases": [
   "ads performance",
   "hourly ads",
   "sponsored ads hourly",
   "marketing stream",
   "stream v2",
   "dayparting",
   "ppc hourly"
  ],
  "caveats": [
   "Sum disjoint rows: traffic and conversions of one entity can sit on separate rows.",
   "searchTerm '(Other)' rows hold impressions only (Amazon's reporting threshold).",
   "Hours and days are the marketplace's own; window_start_utc is the hour as an instant. Dayparting is GROUP BY weekday, hour.",
   "Metrics outside the typed ones (DSP fees, multi-touch, Kindle …) are in `extra`, by Amazon's field id, only when non-zero.",
   "Typed since 2026-11-13: combined_*, long_term_sales, branded_searches*, brand_store_page_views*, add_to_list* and product_review_page_visits*. A row written (or last rebuilt) before then has them NULL and the value in `extra` under Amazon's field id: read COALESCE(column, (extra->>'metric.<fieldId>')::numeric). A read of the old key alone, extra__metric.combinedSales and the like, misses every newer row: read the typed column, combined_sales and the like, instead.",
   "matched_target (Sponsored Display's matched product) is typed since 2026-11-13; a row written (or last rebuilt) before then has it NULL and in dims_extra->>'matchedTarget.value'.",
   "A tombstone (is_tombstone) is a record Amazon deleted: every metric is NULL, so SUM ignores it; filter it out of row listings.",
   "Conversions mature over attribution_window_days and Amazon restates them for 70 days.",
   "Never add a Stream number to a v3 (rpt_sp_* / rpt_sb_* / rpt_sd_*) number.",
   "For a daily or coarser grain prefer the daily tables or a v_ads_* view.",
   "History still loading: a new subscription delivers the dataset's last 70 days over its first 48 hours, so earlier days may be missing until then (Admin → Health lists the accounts)."
  ],
  "pii": false,
  "queryable": true,
  "deprecated": false,
  "strategy": "stream",
  "date_column": "report_date",
  "unique_key": [
   "store_id",
   "country_code",
   "report_date",
   "hour",
   "record_key"
  ],
  "cron": null,
  "retention_days": 75,
  "retention_note": "kept 75 days by report_date; older rows are pruned",
  "marketplace": {
   "grain": "per_mkt",
   "label": {
    "kind": "requested",
    "column": "country_code",
    "values": null,
    "means": "marketplace",
    "nullable": false,
    "null_means": "unplaced"
   }
  }
 },
